--TEST--
`Core\Process::run` is refused by a configuration that writes `exec = []`, and the message names the member and the capability an operator would have to grant — `rule:security/process-exec-capability`, `rule:security/capability-question-is-grant-and-scope`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A CLI run starts any program when `process.exec` is not written. This
// configuration writes it as an empty list, which grants nothing, so the
// written key replaces the default whole.
//
// The target is this case's own source file, which exists and is readable, so
// nothing about the path can be what refuses. A member that asked the
// filesystem first would answer something else here.
try {
    var $result = Core\Process::run("./case.nvs", []);
    echo "accepted: exit=", $result->exitCode(),
         " out=", Core\Bytes::length($result->stdout()),
         " err=", Core\Bytes::length($result->stderr()), "\n";
} catch (IOError $os) {
    echo "the os answered first\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $refused) {
    // The half an operator acts on: which member, and which capability to
    // grant. The path is in the message too and is not asserted, because it is
    // the case folder's own spelling.
    if (Core\Str::contains($refused->message, "Core\\Process::run needs the capability `process.exec` for ")) {
        echo "refused, naming process.exec\n";
    } else {
        echo "refused, saying something else\n";
    }
}

// A bare name is refused the same way, before it is looked up on `PATH`.
try {
    Core\Process::run("git", ["--version"]);
    echo "git: accepted\n";
} catch (IOError $os) {
    echo "git: the os answered first\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $refused) {
    if (Core\Str::contains($refused->message, "exec = [\"git\"]")) {
        echo "git: refused, naming the line to add\n";
    } else {
        echo "git: refused, saying something else\n";
    }
}

// The grant that *is* present still works, so what the blocks above prove is a
// denial and not an unreadable configuration.
if (Core\IO::exists("case.nvs")) {
    echo "fs.read: granted\n";
} else {
    echo "fs.read: not granted\n";
}
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.fs]
read = ["."]

[capabilities.process]
exec = []
--EXPECT--
refused, naming process.exec
git: refused, naming the line to add
fs.read: granted
